CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member initialized via delegation: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ scalar initialized via delegation: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/6 -- delegating-constructor recognition used
to be declaration-order dependent: a delegating constructor declared
BEFORE its target was not recognized (the detector scanned the class's
constructor components, not yet visible), so members were
default-initialized instead; with a non-default-constructible member
this was a hard CONVERSION ERROR ("found no match" for a zero-argument
constructor).  Root cause of the goto_program.cpp dog-food failure
(goto_programt::instructiont's delegating default constructor).  Fixed
by recognizing the delegation by name against the class's
injected-class-name ([class.base.init]/2, [class.pre]).
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
